('c9a2aeeb-79fe-544d-89c6-da7371fc2818'::uuid,'est','"Sequences, Complex Numbers & Advanced Algebra"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"Which of the following sets of numbers has the property that the sum of any two numbers in the set is also a number in the set?\nI. The set of even integers\nII. The set of odd integers\nIII. The set of prime numbers"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"I only"},{"key":"G","text":"III only"},{"key":"H","text":"I and II only"},{"key":"J","text":"I and III only"},{"key":"K","text":"I, II, and III"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t10.md","source_sha256":"f20516078371096927f6322b82ff1576ab3861b0fb64e776ba5ff7fbc66dbac0","source_question_id":"T10-06","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Sequences, Complex Numbers & Advanced Algebra"}'::jsonb,'"F"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t10.md (T10-06)."'::jsonb),
('d8cbbf97-f460-5034-be57-b56ca9b42ea0'::uuid,'est','"Triangles, Trigonometry & Similarity"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"A circle in the standard (x,y) coordinate plane is tangent to the x-axis at 4 and tangent to the y-axis at 4. Which of the following is an equation of the circle?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"x² + y² = 4"},{"key":"B","text":"x² + y² = 16"},{"key":"C","text":"(x − 4)² + (y − 4)² = 4"},{"key":"D","text":"(x − 4)² + (y − 4)² = 16"},{"key":"E","text":"(x + 4)² + (y + 4)² = 16"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t10.md","source_sha256":"f20516078371096927f6322b82ff1576ab3861b0fb64e776ba5ff7fbc66dbac0","source_question_id":"T10-07","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Triangles, Trigonometry & Similarity"}'::jsonb,'"D"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t10.md (T10-07)."'::jsonb),
('ac661305-46a4-589a-94d9-5268064a56b7'::uuid,'est','"Sequences, Complex Numbers & Advanced Algebra"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"Which of the following is the solution set for all real numbers x such that x − 2 < x − 5 ?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"The empty set"},{"key":"B","text":"The set containing all real numbers"},{"key":"C","text":"The set containing all negative real numbers"},{"key":"D","text":"The set containing all nonnegative real numbers"},{"key":"E","text":"The set containing only zero"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t10.md","source_sha256":"f20516078371096927f6322b82ff1576ab3861b0fb64e776ba5ff7fbc66dbac0","source_question_id":"T10-08","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Sequences, Complex Numbers & Advanced Algebra"}'::jsonb,'"A"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t10.md (T10-08)."'::jsonb),
('97c60bb1-785c-5525-be9e-61ce7eb732e1'::uuid,'est','"Plane Geometry, Measurement & Transformations"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"[Figure: Graph of g(x) = √x starting at the origin, rising to the right.]\nThe figure shown represents the function g(x) = √x. Suppose h(x) is a transformation of g(x) and is given by the equation h(x) = √(x + 1) + 3. Which of the following correctly states the domain and range of h(x)?"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"F","text":"Domain: x ≥ −1; Range: y ≥ 0"},{"key":"G","text":"Domain: x ≥ −1; Range: y ≥ 3"},{"key":"H","text":"Domain: x ≥ 0; Range: y ≥ 0"},{"key":"J","text":"Domain: x ≥ 1; Range: y ≥ −3"},{"key":"K","text":"Domain: x ≥ 1; Range: y ≥ 3"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t10.md","source_sha256":"f20516078371096927f6322b82ff1576ab3861b0fb64e776ba5ff7fbc66dbac0","source_question_id":"T10-09","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Plane Geometry, Measurement & Transformations"}'::jsonb,'"G"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t10.md (T10-09)."'::jsonb),
