('249bee5b-74b2-51c4-a79f-e94f929dfc5f'::uuid,'est','"Sequences, Complex Numbers & Advanced Algebra"'::jsonb,'medium','mcq','"One of the following graphs illustrates the solution set to the inequality |x − a| ≤ 3 for some positive a. Which one?\n[Figure: five number lines labeled with −a−3, a−3, a+3. A: shaded segment between a−3 and a+3 (closed dots). B: shaded between −a−3 and a+3. C: shaded left of a+3 only. D: shaded outside (left of −a−3 and right of a+3). E: shaded right of a−3.]"'::jsonb,'[{"key":"A","text":"Graph A"},{"key":"B","text":"Graph B"},{"key":"C","text":"Graph C"},{"key":"D","text":"Graph D"},{"key":"E","text":"Graph E"}]'::jsonb,'{"source":"Kimi Agent Math PDF Question Bank (4)","source_file":"book_t10.md","source_sha256":"f20516078371096927f6322b82ff1576ab3861b0fb64e776ba5ff7fbc66dbac0","source_question_id":"T10-32","import_batch":"est2-kimi-bank-2026-09-21","curriculum_lesson":"Sequences, Complex Numbers & Advanced Algebra"}'::jsonb,'"A"'::jsonb,'"Source-keyed answer from book_t10.md (T10-32)."'::jsonb),
